cards.body:
The float-equality lint no longer fires, and `tests/ui_lint/float_eq_warn.jet` fails with "should emit at least one lint".

Root cause is exact-by-default. The fixture compares `1.0 == 2.0`, and under D-TYPE2-DEFAULT1 a bare decimal literal is now an exact `Decimal`, so that comparison is exact and the lint is right to stay quiet.

But the lint does not fire for a genuine Float either. All of these are silent under `jet check`:

    x :: Float{1.0}
    y :: Float{2.0}
    if x == y :> print("equal")

    fn approx(a: Float, b: Float) Bool :> a == b

    x :: Float{1.0}
    y :: x + Float{1.0}
    if x == y :> print("equal")

So the lint appears unreachable rather than merely narrowed. Either it lost its trigger when the numeric default moved, or it was only ever matching the literal shape that is now Decimal.

Decide which is true and make the lint fire for approximate comparison, then restore the fixture to a shape that exercises it. Do not delete the lint to make the test pass: comparing two Floats for exact equality is the classic numeric bug this exists to catch, and exact-by-default makes the remaining Float cases the ones that most need warning.

