## Goal
Publish a signed Jet toolchain channel at `dl.jet-lang.dev` and make `jet self update` resolve, verify and install from it without ever writing over a running executable.

## Current state
The client and publisher are already implemented in the shipped host:
- `Source/main.rs:6718` `run_self_update` calls `crates/jetpack/src/ToolchainUpdate.rs`:
  - `configured_endpoint` `:112`;
  - `run` `:229`;
  - manifest and signature parsing `:388,732,754`;
  - release policy (expiry, freshness, downgrade, monotonic sequence) `:507-585,1675`;
  - https-only redirect policy `:962`;
  - stage-beside install, fsync, rollback and health check `:1431-1760`;
  - the Windows helper `:1770-1792`.
- Rust unit tests `:2300-2572` cover:
  - `signed_channel_and_keyless_channel_are_distinct_explicit_tiers`;
  - `keyless_override_is_local_only`;
  - `digest_failure_leaves_current_executable_unchanged`;
  - `install_replaces_current_path_without_backup_or_partial_file`;
  - `manifest_policy_rejects_expired_future_stale_and_downgrade`;
  - `monotonic_state_rejects_a_replayed_sequence`.
- Publication tooling is `Tools/jetpack-infra/stage-toolchain.sh`, and `Tools/jetpack-infra/test-toolchain-update.sh` is the end-to-end local-file proof (signed, keyless E2105, corrupt E2105/digest, cross-platform apply refusal).
- Schema and fixtures live in `Docs/site/dist/dl/` (the plan's `site/dist/dl` is stale). The spec is `Docs/spec/packaging/toolchain-channel.md`, and E2105 is in `crates/jet-codegen/src/Prelude/Diagnostics.jet:814`.
- The only thing missing is the live channel for criterion 1. It needs #2199 publication, the production toolchain key and owner DNS/TLS/hosting under D-DOMAIN-LAYOUT1=A. The Jet port of this code is #3652 (Recipe area), which is not a prerequisite here.

## Changes
1. No new client code. Fix the stale paths (`tools/` → `Tools/`, `site/` → `Docs/site/`, `docs/` → `Docs/`) in the channel spec if any remain.
2. After #2199 and the owner publication gate: stage `/v1/stable/manifest.json`, signed sidecars and artifacts with `stage-toolchain.sh` using the production toolchain key, and publish them at `https://dl.jet-lang.dev`. The default endpoint then resolves them.

## Proof
- `Tools/agent/jet-env cargo test -p jetpack --lib ToolchainUpdate::`: every ToolchainUpdate unit test passes (criteria 2-5).
- `Tools/agent/jet-env sh Tools/jetpack-infra/test-toolchain-update.sh` prints `toolchain self-update and publisher boundary proofs passed`.
- After publication: `jet self update --dry-run` with the default endpoint prints `verified jet <v> for <target> from https://dl.jet-lang.dev` (criterion 1).

## Batch
batch-host-cli: the proof is the shipped `jet self update` host command.

## Dependencies
#2199 (trust root publication).

